      "item": "tribalpower:wake_bell",
      "text": [
        "The Seal-carvers' craft: a bell that mourns the dead. Every creature that dies near it pays Pulse into its reservoir, so a mob farm becomes a power plant."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How it pays",
      "text": [
        "A death within **16 blocks** pays **20 Pulse** for a hostile and **5** for a passive creature. Players' deaths pay nothing.",
        "Deaths fill a reservoir of **2,000**, which the bell lets out at most **8 a second** unranked. Ranking adds **15% Pulse a second** per rank. A big farm fills the reservoir and then idles; anything past the brim is lost.",
        "Only the **nearest** bell hears a death, so stacking bells buys nothing. A bell paused by redstone hears nothing at all."
      ]
    },
